Learning goals
By the end of this week, you should be able to:

distinguish context-window capacity from effective context use;
explain the lost-in-the-middle finding at a conceptual level;
identify irrelevant, stale, conflicting, and missing context;
use a compact context brief to stabilise a long task;
recognise when a fresh session or context reset is preferable to continued prompting;
